    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build succeeds. The full suite consists of the `AcceptanceTest` (3 tests), all green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI introduced address normalization for owner creation, mirroring the existing `OwnerTelephone`/`OwnerEmail` helper pattern.\n\n**New helper** \u2014 `OwnerAddress.java`:\n- `normalize(String)`: trims and collapses internal whitespace, upper-cases, and expands whole-token abbreviations `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`. Returns `null` when the input is null or blank after normalization.\n- `forComparison(String)`: same normalization but maps null/blank to `\"\"` so addressless owners compare equal.\n\n**Behaviour changes** across the `POST /api/owners` pipeline:\n- `ValidateOwnerFields` \u2014 normalizes the address first, adds `\"address\"` to the required-field errors when it is blank *after* normalization (so `\"   \"` \u2192 400), and stores the normalized value back on the body so it is persisted and returned.\n- `CheckOwnerHouseholdUnique` \u2014 household duplicate detection now compares addresses via `OwnerAddress.forComparison` on both sides.\n- `AssignHousehold` \u2014 household membership matching and the derived shared `householdId` now use the same normalized address form.\n\nVerified against the acceptance tests: `\"  12  main  st \"` \u2192 `\"12 MAIN STREET\"`, `\"7 elm ave\"` \u2192 `\"7 ELM AVENUE\"`, and a whitespace-only address is rejected with 400.",
